{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5cf60483-cda5-550a-8ccd-54acfa5d1d22",
    "name": "SCRUM-127 Risk context",
    "description": "Manual checks for GET /api/properties/id/{id}/location-intelligence/risk. No token needed. Variables: baseUrl and one property id per case: idSfha (parcel point inside a FEMA SFHA polygon), idZoneX (zone X), idOpenWater (sea tract, no NRI row), idNoPolygon (no FEMA polygon at the point), idNoParcel (property without parcel), idNoStorms (no located NOAA event within 10 km), idCountyNotLoaded (county whose flood map is not loaded), idInvalid (0), idUnknown. The defaults match the local verification of 2026-11-24 (docs/location-intelligence-risk.md); on another database pick ids with SELECTs on parcels, flood_zones and census_tracts.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 Inside a Special Flood Hazard Area (200, flood AVAILABLE)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/properties/id/{{idSfha}}/location-intelligence/risk",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "properties",
            "id",
            "{{idSfha}}",
            "location-intelligence",
            "risk"
          ]
        },
        "description": "A property whose parcel point lies inside a FEMA AE/A/V polygon."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const r = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('top status AVAILABLE', () => pm.expect(r.status).to.eql('AVAILABLE'));",
              "pm.test('flood zone with SFHA true', () => { pm.expect(r.flood.status).to.eql('AVAILABLE'); pm.expect(r.flood.zone).to.be.a('string'); pm.expect(r.flood.specialFloodHazardArea).to.eql(true); });",
              "pm.test('hazards: tract, version and 8 ratings', () => { pm.expect(r.hazards.status).to.eql('AVAILABLE'); pm.expect(r.hazards.tractFips).to.have.lengthOf(11); pm.expect(r.hazards.ratings).to.have.lengthOf(8); pm.expect(r.hazards.ratings[0].code).to.eql('HRCN'); });",
              "pm.test('storms: counts within radius and county', () => { pm.expect(r.storms.status).to.eql('AVAILABLE'); pm.expect(r.storms.radius).to.eql(10000); pm.expect(r.storms.fromYear).to.eql(1996); pm.expect(r.storms.eventsWithinRadius).to.be.above(0); pm.expect(r.storms.eventsInCounty).to.be.at.least(r.storms.eventsWithinRadius); });",
              "pm.test('every block has source and dataAsOf', () => ['flood','hazards','storms'].forEach(k => { const b = pm.response.json()[k]; pm.expect(b.source, k).to.be.a('string'); if (b.status !== 'NO_COVERAGE') pm.expect(b.dataAsOf, k).to.match(/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/); }));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 Zone X (200, SFHA false, no elevation)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/properties/id/{{idZoneX}}/location-intelligence/risk",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
